# arvo-capacity

A count fixed when the consumer builds, carried as a type, that sizes real arrays from code generic over it.

`Capacity` projects an array of exactly its count, which generic code reads and writes as a slice, and
`Dim<N>` is the capacity of `N` elements. Many capacities bundle as the associated types of one
parameter, one nests inside another with no product computed, and `count` reads a capacity's count in a
constant as an `arvo_numeral::USize` under the adaptation the consumer names. Nothing about it needs a
feature line in the consumer.

Builds on `arvo-format` and `arvo-numeral`. `no_std`, no allocation, nothing at run time but the arrays.

## Status

Unreleased, at 0.0.0. The source implements what is described here and its tests pass, and the surface
may still change before a first release.
